Point /WHOLEARCHIVE at the library the linker can actually find under ninja

node.exe, node_mksnapshot.exe, cctest and embedtest link several static libraries
through MSVC's /WHOLEARCHIVE so nothing in them is dropped as unused. node.gyp and
node.gypi write those flags as <(PRODUCT_DIR)/lib/<name>.lib, which is where the
MSBuild generator puts a static library. This build uses --ninja, and the ninja
generator puts them under obj/<its directory>/ instead, so the first link that got
that far failed on a file nobody creates:

    [4222/4233] LINK_EMBED node_mksnapshot.exe
    LINK : fatal error LNK1356: cannot find library `lib/zlib.lib' specified to be whole archived

Nothing else complained because the real obj/... libraries are already inputs of the
same link step - only this flag string pointed somewhere else.

Node already keeps three spellings of the same library side by side: xcode_settings
for Xcode, msvs_settings for MSBuild, and ldflags using <(obj_dir) for GNU ld. The
msvs_settings one was simply never written for a ninja generator. common.gypi already
branches on GENERATOR == "ninja" to define obj_dir, so the same test chooses the right
spelling here, and a build that uses MSBuild keeps the flags it has today unchanged.

